Author: Eduard Arbona <175124143+earbona23@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Wed Nov 4 23:10:33 2026 -0400

    fix(graph): cache a paged response under its own request's key

    Complete-Result read the request uri from the enclosing scope. The batch path
    completes its responses in end{}, after the loop in process{} that builds the
    requests has ended, so the only uri still in scope is the last request's. Every
    paged response in a batch was cached under the key of the last request, and the
    request it belonged to was never cached: a later call for that last uri is
    served another request's objects. Pass the key of the request the response
    belongs to instead, kept beside the request list so it never reaches the batch
    body.

    Invoke-MtGraphRequestCache skipped the cache read on -DisableCache but still
    wrote the response. The paging loop reads every page with the cache off because
    a skip token is not always unique, so each page was cached anyway: a three-page
    request left three entries instead of one, and a caller that asked to bypass the
    cache populated it for the next caller. Gate the write on -DisableCache as the
    read already is. The GET and runHuntingQuery write branches were identical and
    are now one.

